      "message": "In this CL, we added a speed feature `adaptive_cdef_mode` to disable CDEF adaptively for low complexity decode.\n\nThe speed feature always disables chroma CDEF by forcing zero filter strength during the joint luma-chroma strength search. This is achieved by setting the MSE at chroma strength index 0 to zero and all non-zero strength indices to 1 before the search, so that zero filter strength always wins for chroma due to least cost, without evaluating chroma MSE.\n\nFor luma, CDEF is disabled when the MSE improvement over zero filter strength falls below a threshold of 4%, indicating that CDEF filtering is not beneficial for the current frame. This logic is not applied for `pyramid_level\u003d1` frames (KEY and ARF frames) and luma CDEF is always applied for these frames.\n\nPerformance results of encoder and decoder for streams generated with low complexity decode enabled, measured w.r.t a baseline with CDEF disabled (`--enable-cdef\u003d0`).\n\n```\n                      Instruction Count        Time\n                         Reduction(%)      Reduction(%)                    BD-Rate Loss(%)\ncpu   Resolution      Encoder    Decoder     Decoder      avg.psnr    ssim     vmaf    vmaf_neg    uvq_1p5\n 1    SHORTS608P      -0.012     -3.039       -2.828      -0.2752   -0.3140   -0.5407   -0.2830    -8.0127\n 1    SHORTS720P      -0.013     -3.934       -3.414      -0.3704   -0.4590   -0.6669   -0.3683    -8.6858\n 1   SHORTS1080P      -0.120     -5.729       -5.468      -0.5310   -0.8579   -0.5073   -0.4236    -9.5319\n 1        HDRES2      -0.262     -2.943       -2.961      -0.2168    0.0478   -0.5655   -0.4409    -9.0657\n 1      UGCHDRES      -0.078     -3.901       -4.189      -0.4257   -0.3742   -0.5712   -0.5143    -9.3248\n 1       Average      -0.092     -3.946       -3.771      -0.3647   -0.4090   -0.5705   -0.3967    -8.8893\n \n 2    SHORTS608P      -0.492     -3.416       -3.164      -0.3297   -0.4261   -0.3052   -0.1471   -10.2164\n 2